6ff942eecc83603f861eb922c3864e9578b9c13ec9c95b27b0f07b7cfa32\",\"source_size_bytes\":5161,\"total_source_bytes\":null}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Anchored provenance-local source register\nNON-AUTHORITATIVE, INCOMPLETE SEMANTIC RESIDUE. Omission is not evidence that a source or requirement was covered. Exact sources remain reopenable.\n\n## CLAIM MANDATE-001\nSLOT_SOURCE: MANDATE\nSOURCE_VERSION: df5e0ae25a22101747f338fe585656baf46dd1dbf02669fbc7400544c03dcd4a\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-001\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: Only network control may authorize an engineering movement\nANCHOR_BYTES: 151-209\nANCHOR_SHA256: 085abc73735679fc3094fc28cb631c58f63fe3faf39d3f7e876530ef1436981c\nCONTEXT_LINES: 5-5\nCONTEXT_SHA256: 799fb01431001de261aadfebed7a3600bd70ab3db1a15e7264eec8b32fb69c1b\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: The MANDATE source states that only network control may authorize an engineering movement.\n\n## CLAIM MANDATE-002\nSLOT_SOURCE: MANDATE\nSOURCE_VERSION: df5e0ae25a22101747f338fe585656baf46dd1dbf02669fbc7400544c03dcd4a\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-001\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: only the rail-safety director may authorize passenger service\nANCHOR_BYTES: 215-276\nANCHOR_SHA256: 98bcd7a27d556e7f6bc61dd0b1faf69b93685f1bffd5c7f442535d57c5ff2d9b\nCONTEXT_LINES: 5-5\nCONTEXT_SHA256: 799fb01431001de261aadfebed7a3600bd70ab3db1a15e7264eec8b32fb69c1b\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: The MANDATE source states that only the rail-safety director may authorize passenger service.\n\n## CLAIM PWR-001\nSLOT_SOURCE: POWER\nSOURCE_VERSION: fce863b5472f7d368c3b4e8db0391b4a083e633d52694997dc3b767f90349157\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-004\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: Installed traction capacity is 34.0 megawatts, while current usable capacity after feeder derating is 26.5 megawatts\nANCHOR_BYTES: 73-189\nANCHOR_SHA256: 7198849a1f47a163ec3270c14024935c5b5a82b0a4b1e391cba12b85b86152bb\nCONTEXT_LINES: 5-5\nCONTEXT_SHA256: 7e99c7d7cd676beca4f42b249b07b28676db7f8fdc13641cd02dbaf3a9437599\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: The installed traction capacity is 34.0 megawatts and the current usable capacity after feeder derating is 26.5 megawatts.\n\n## CLAIM PWR-002\nSLOT_SOURCE: POWER\nSOURCE_VERSION: fce863b5472f7d368c3b4e8db0391b4a083e633d52694997dc3b767f90349157\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-004\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: Feeder voltage is 24.7 kilovolts and must remain between 24.0 and 25.2 kilovolts at every monitored node for three consecutive fifteen-minute windows\nANCHOR_BYTES: 260-409\nANCHOR_SHA256: 71f4f3ae1e7333d0d6289c42e079bbb28e13ba024cac3cd4451e1e8a78d0c5f9\nCONTEXT_LINES: 6-6\nCONTEXT_SHA256: f73f18942e2f605e94b6e751f1ef45e404d9f56a798d65cfb67f946c679b9215\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: The feeder voltage is 24.7 kilovolts and must remain between 24.0 and 25.2 kilovolts at every monitored node for three consecutive fifteen-minute windows.\n\n## CLAIM PWR-003\nSLOT_SOURCE: POWER\nSOURCE_VERSION: fce863b5472f7d368c3b4e8db0391b4a083e633d52694997dc3b767f90349157\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-004\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: The backup plant carries 11.8 megawatts for eighteen hours at current fuel stock; it does not carry full passenger peak and eighteen hours is not eighteen days\nANCHOR_BYTES: 460-619\nANCHOR_SHA256: 2f6411a594dfe9901bd373c306057576ae894b81af615a575197cac947e5b2b7\nCONTEXT_LINES: 7-7\nCONTEXT_SHA256: 1935f5b3982a737340be4a04a3a1e78760db2973e6a7e19b8f3173bf030a3262\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: The backup plant carries 11.8 megawatts for eighteen hours at current fuel stock, does not carry full passenger peak, and the duration is eighteen hours rather than eighteen days.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Current Keystone lifecycle phase\nPhase: construction. Build exact task work and use `begin_verification` only after the frozen mechanical construction milestone is met.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_source\",\"end_line\":86,\"source_id\":\"TELEMETRY\",\"start_line\":1}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"source:TELEMETRY:1-86\",\"object_version\":\"4c1bef4a93d7df8167a8b1a290697972feb2b3ff881c3758a7214b3ee2035d71\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-010\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"end_line\":86,\"source_id\":\"TELEMETRY\",\"source_path\":\"sources/TELEMETRY_COVERAGE.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"4c1bef4a93d7df8167a8b1a290697972feb2b3ff881c3758a7214b3ee2035d71\",\"source_size_bytes\":5120,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Monitoring coverage, alarms, and delivery latency\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent critical-signal coverage is 93 percent; seven percent remains unobserved. Coverage is not confidence and does not prove uninstrumented assets healthy.\nRoute-state delivery is 720 milliseconds at p95 and 1,180 milliseconds at p99. These are observations, not response deadlines.\nThe power warning threshold is 24.2 kilovolts and the operating stop is 23.8 kilovolts. Warning and stop semantics must remain distinct.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nTRACK, SIGNAL, POWER, ROLLING, and WEATHER rely on TELEMETRY observations while retaining their own gates and authorities.\nCOMMS may report state only where coverage and source currency are adequate.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| TEL-000 | track-circuits | v4 | 93.0 | percent-coverage | superseded |\n| TEL-001 | voltage | v4 | 94.9 | percent-coverage | current |\n| TEL-002 | wind | v4 | 93.7 | percent-covera