\nPreserve coverage uncertainty, percentile latency, voltage, purpose, and currentness.\nDefine alternate observation routes and evidence for retiring manual watches.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_source\",\"end_line\":86,\"source_id\":\"LOADS\",\"start_line\":1}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"source:LOADS:1-86\",\"object_version\":\"47fd04643fa8de992686f6cae89cc861488f99b9320bc00596cefbbf86084be6\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-011\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"end_line\":86,\"source_id\":\"LOADS\",\"source_path\":\"sources/LOADS_FREIGHT.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"47fd04643fa8de992686f6cae89cc861488f99b9320bc00596cefbbf86084be6\",\"source_size_bytes\":4959,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Freight, hazardous materials, and axle restrictions\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nRiver-bridge temporary axle load is limited to 20.5 tonnes. The normal 23.0-tonne rating is suspended and cannot govern the current candidate.\nHazardous-material consist H71 requires a 600-meter separation from passenger platforms and an independent route clearance before movement.\nA consist, axle map, bridge inspection, route, cargo classification, or separation-plan change makes earlier freight clearance stale.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nTRACK supplies bridge and route state, SIGNAL supplies route locking, and MANDATE separates freight from passenger authority.\nPASSENGER plans must preserve H71 separation and COMMS must not disclose protected cargo details.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| LOD-000 | hazmat-71 | v4 | 20.0 | tonnes-axle | superseded |\n| LOD-001 | grain-22 | v4 | 21.9 | tonnes-axle | current |\n| LOD-002 | intermodal-9 | v4 | 20.7 | tonnes-axle | current |\n| LOD-003 | bridge-axle | v4 | 22.6 | tonnes-axle | current |\n| LOD-004 | hazmat-71 | v4 | 21.4 | tonnes-axle | c